en how close  i am to finishing the series but while  we're on things like that there was not  just one but two  quote special chapters during the  shibuya rock both of which came at  wonderfully hugely inappropriate times  just as we were about to settle things  and i'm guessing akutami was under an  exceptional amount of pressure at this  point missing deadlines and such and as  a result he had to pump out the  short short chapters with big big panels  you know very low  production value stuff and yes they were  they were fun to read because the  characters of jiu-jitsu kaisen are just  fun in general it's just that they came  at the worst  possible time right when yuji vs majito  was about to end ah mahito that's that's  where i started that's what i was  talking about like i said his part in  the arc intersects with just about  everyone and another huge factor would  be kugisaki because  damn was she glorious during the sock i  love the way that she handed mojito's  ass to him with resonance and it very  much highlights what i love about power  systems like this because  one matchup of weird abilities that can  really be the end of you and she was  glorious  right up until the end i suppose now  that was a shock a character like naomi  yeah sure i can expect him to die he's a  mental figure after all and mental  figures are  practically cursed today but kugisaki  man she's the next generation her death  pretty seriously rocked me to my core  and it was such a  magnificent way for her to go out with  her last words and everything  i am sad shocked but satisfied now with  that said  please please please let her stay dead  might sound like a harsh thing to say  but this was such a brilliant moment do  not undercut it by having some dude  state that look her chances of being  alive aren't  zero percent maybe that just gives me  the worst sinking feeling in the world  and if this was most other shown series  i would take that as practically a  guarantee that she will survive  i guess the thing about jujutsu kaisen  is that akitami does handle death and  resurrection even  pretty well like the toji example so if  kukisaki does come back into the story  then i'm willing to think that there's a  satisfying and hopefully costly way to  do so but please no outright  resurrections i beg of you  back to mahito though actually no let's  talk about yuji he reaches  a thorough breaking point during shibuya  one that i thought would be taking him  to a very dark place however luckily he  happens to have a supportive alter  brother and todo does make his glorious  presence known i was wondering where he  was during the first half but he is used  to  absolute perfection here he's such a  good foil for mahito and a great  supporting presence for yuji and there  were just too many great todo moments in  his short tenure to name here  would be a very long list but my  favorite is undoubtedly when he pulled  the old clap trick right at the end  claiming that applause is the  accumulation of the soul distracting  mahito and allowing yuji to do the thing  and all i'm going to say is at this  moment it was  very isaac natural no spoilers from  hunter hunter but very similar vibes and  yeah toto absolutely  makes this fight it's a great escalation  of when he and yuji took on hanumi  and just super satisfying to read but to  actually discuss majito  i've left him to the end because i'm  honestly kind of underwhelmed by him and  in retrospect  that was probably the point the thing i  disliked most was his final form because  final forms  always look like garbage and he is no  exception we abandoned his cool  patchwork design to assume this  is really sort of standard curse thing  which had absolutely no character about  it whatsoever and at that point it might  as well have been yuji fighting any  miscellaneous super special curse dude  because really the crowning feature of  mahito is his emotion and facial  expression sort of like how i said at  least 50 percent of goja's character is  purely in his hands well the same  applies to mahi toba with his face so  once you take away that face and replace  it with this  fleshy wall with a sort of mouth he just  became  insanely boring and that state it was a  really pitiful climax to what had been  such a compelling character and once  again yeah that may very well be  intentional because the big revelation  at the end of this arc is that yes  mojito was more or less meaningless he  was  essentially a delicious snack he was  there to be grown like livestock and  then consumed by  the ghetto okay ghetto not ghetto  noritoshikamo  not him either though i don't know he  has many names apparently this is where  the bombardment of information was  really taken to the extreme so firstly i  do love the idea that this entire saga  of jiu-jitsu kaisen has been a mere  portion of some sort of grander plan to  do with the ghetto figure he certainly  did  eyes and the hell out of this story and  these last few chapters just ceded so  much insane crap like that little moment  of cutting to samiki with the stuff on  her head  saying stuff like all cursed objects  have now been unsealed and a wild  revelatory statement like  like adjusting brains is that what he  did adjusting brains for sorcery and  vessel strength and all sorts of madness  not even going to pretend that i have  taken everything in because ghetto  said a lot of things i'm definitely  gonna have to go back on it all i know  is that allegedly we are returning to  the world of haiyan there's a  maximum uzumaki and the golden age of  cursed techniques is upon us and very  frustratingly this is where the ark  seems to  officially end so i legitimately have no  idea where we're going from here what i  do know is that this arc was a very  bitter defeat  after all of this we didn't save gojo we  lost very lovable characters like nanami  kugisaki mekamaru actually he had a very  touching goodbye and did we ever find  out what happened to maki and nobito  didn't they get like the crap burnt out  of them too the villains we thought we  were fighting were not  really the villains like i i did feel  for the nature cursed spirit gang  they were pricks more specifically jogo  was a prick but they weren't evil at  heart  and now the world has been immeasurably  ruined by a big bad  actually evil dude and all i can say is  that thankfully at least we still have  panda so there is some hope here i mean  i haven't even spoken about choso either  to be fair  he didn't really do anything unexpected  and very happy to have him as what i  think  is an ally now but he's cool and so  that's that and also there's probably a  million other things i haven't mentioned  either because this is a review remember  not an analysis but shibuya  utter insanity this arc simultaneously  paid everything off that was set up for  it as well as set up an incredible  amount to come after it the story the  interactions the combat all of it was  fascinating and jujitsu  sin deserves all of the accumulation of  soul-based applause for pulling off  its first major narrative climax but  that pretty much does it for this blind  review of jiu-jitsu  sen shibuya incident dark and what do  you guys think please do leave your  thoughts in the comments below or even  join my discord server and if you're  keen for some more jiu jitsu sorcery  then please do check out some of my  other videos or even subscribe to the  channel for very maybe  regular jujutsu morbidity delivered  straight into your youtube feed but for  now this has been the new world review  and i'm going to go and lie down
 

